<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16132" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσεβ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be impious, act profanely, commit sacrilege,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.159
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδικέω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				367
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐς τὸν νηόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.129
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				490
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.93
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὰ ἱρά, τοὺς θεούς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.139
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				4.1.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὰ θεῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					13.16
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀσέβημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					910e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγγελίας καὶ ἐπιτάξεις παρὰ
				νόμον ἀ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				941a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ οὗ τὴν ἑορτὴν ἀσεβῶν ἕαλωκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.227
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc. pers.,
				<i>sin against,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ θεὸν ἢ ξένον τιν᾽ ἀσεβῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					271
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.77
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.291c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἱαρὸν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.2418
				</span></i>
			 (Thebes, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν Καίσαρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1612.23
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσεβοῦνται οι&lt;&gt;
				θεοί</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				2.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠσεβῆσθαι πρός τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					57.9
				</span></i>
			; of households, <i>to be affected with the consequences of
				sin,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν τις ἀσεβηθῇ τῶν οἴκων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					877e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Pass.
			 also of the act, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμοὶ ἠσέβηται οὐδὲν περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἠσεβημένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					6.6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
